    <h2 class="pd-title">Freight Forwarders Liability Insurance (FFL)</h2>
    <section class="pd-broker-note" aria-label="Insurance broker note">
      <div class="pd-broker-icon" aria-hidden="true">⚖</div>
      <div class="pd-broker-body">
        <span class="pd-broker-tag">From a licensed insurance broker</span>
        <p class="pd-broker-text">
          <strong>N2N Insurance Brokerage</strong> does not represent any single insurer — it <strong>independently represents the client</strong>
          as an FSS-registered broker (Reg. No. 2026-012201). We compare the wordings, rates and service of AIG · Chubb · DB · Hyundai · KB · Meritz
          to propose the <strong>cover and price best suited to your risk</strong>. Each insurer's full wording is provided at application and binding.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>
    <div class="pd-tabs" role="tablist">
      <button class="pd-tab-btn active" data-tab="tab1" role="tab">Overview</button>
      <button class="pd-tab-btn" data-tab="tab2" role="tab">Cover</button>
      <button class="pd-tab-btn" data-tab="tab3" role="tab">How to apply</button>
    </div>

    <section id="tab1" class="pd-tab-pane active" role="tabpanel">
<div class="pd-section"><h3>Overview</h3>
        <p>Freight forwarders liability (FFL) covers a forwarder's or multimodal-transport operator's legal liability for <strong>cargo loss and third-party loss</strong> arising while it receives a shipper's goods and arranges international carriage, transhipment, storage, customs clearance and delivery.</p>
        <p>Cover is built on three pillars — <strong>goods-legal liability</strong> to the shipper, <strong>third-party liability</strong>, and <strong>professional indemnity</strong>. The main insureds are operators issuing KIFFA / FIATA / IATA bills of lading; purely domestic transport is underwritten as a separate line.</p></div>
      <div class="pd-section"><h3>Key features</h3>
        <ul class="pd-feature-list">
          <li><span class="pd-num">01</span><div class="pd-ftext"><strong>Goods-legal liability</strong>
            <p>Liability to shippers for damage, theft, loss or delay to entrusted cargo.</p></div></li>
          <li><span class="pd-num">02</span><div class="pd-ftext"><strong>Third-party liability</strong>
            <p>Bodily injury and property damage to third parties.</p></div></li>
          <li><span class="pd-num">03</span><div class="pd-ftext"><strong>Professional indemnity</strong>
            <p>Errors in advice, documentation and customs handling.</p></div></li>
          <li><span class="pd-num">04</span><div class="pd-ftext"><strong>End-to-end scope</strong>
            <p>Carriage, transhipment, storage and customs combined in one policy.</p></div></li>
        </ul></div>
      <div class="pd-section"><h3>Who needs it</h3>
        <ul class="pd-feature-list">
          <li><span class="pd-num">01</span><div class="pd-ftext"><strong>Multimodal forwarders</strong>
            <p>Operators arranging international transport.</p></div></li>
          <li><span class="pd-num">02</span><div class="pd-ftext"><strong>B/L issuers</strong>
            <p>KIFFA / FIATA / IATA bill-of-lading issuers.</p></div></li>
          <li><span class="pd-num">03</span><div class="pd-ftext"><strong>Agents &amp; NVOCC</strong>
            <p>Air/sea transport agents and NVOCC operators.</p></div></li>
          <li><span class="pd-num">04</span><div class="pd-ftext"><strong>3PL operators</strong>
            <p>Providers combining storage, transport and value-added services.</p></div></li>
        </ul></div>
    </section>
    <section id="tab2" class="pd-tab-pane" role="tabpanel">
<div class="pd-section"><h3>Main losses covered</h3>
        <ul class="pd-bul">
          <li>Compensation to shippers for cargo damage, theft, loss or delay</li>
          <li>Third-party bodily injury and property damage</li>
          <li>Professional advice and documentation errors</li>
          <li>One cover spanning carriage, transhipment, storage and customs</li>
          <li>Incident-handling emergency, litigation and legal costs</li>
        </ul></div>
      <div class="pd-exclude"><h4>Main exclusions</h4>
        <ul>
          <li>Willful misconduct or fraud</li>
          <li>Purely domestic transport (underwritten as a separate line)</li>
          <li>Fines and penalties</li>
          <li>War, terrorism and nuclear risks</li>
        </ul></div>
    </section>
    <section id="tab3" class="pd-tab-pane" role="tabpanel">
<div class="pd-section"><h3>Conditions &amp; process</h3>
        <ul class="pd-bul">
          <li>Designed for operators issuing KIFFA / FIATA / IATA bills of lading</li>
          <li>Purely domestic transport is underwritten as a separate line</li>
          <li>Final terms, limits and premium are confirmed after insurer underwriting</li>
        </ul></div>
      <div class="pd-section"><h3>What we need to quote</h3>
        <ul class="pd-feature-list">
          <li><span class="pd-num">01</span><div class="pd-ftext"><strong>Business profile</strong>
            <p>Modes handled, B/L type and annual turnover.</p></div></li>
          <li><span class="pd-num">02</span><div class="pd-ftext"><strong>Trade lanes</strong>
            <p>Main routes, commodities and traffic volumes.</p></div></li>
          <li><span class="pd-num">03</span><div class="pd-ftext"><strong>Services</strong>
            <p>Storage, customs and value-added services provided.</p></div></li>
          <li><span class="pd-num">04</span><div class="pd-ftext"><strong>Claims history</strong>
            <p>Past cargo or liability claims.</p></div></li>
        </ul></div>
      <div class="pd-section"><h3>Other notes</h3>
        <ul class="pd-bul">
          <li>Cover follows the standard goods-legal / third-party / professional-indemnity structure</li>
          <li>Final terms, limits and premium are confirmed after insurer underwriting</li>
        </ul></div>
    </section>

